  {
    "topic":"Textual-critical tradition and SBLGNT editorial stance",
    "summary":"The repository centers around the digital textual-critical analysis of the Greek New Testament, specifically leveraging resources like the SBLGNT and MorphGNT datasets. It primarily implements data processing pipelines and Python tools (py-sblgnt) for parsing, annotating, and querying morphological and textual variants in the Greek NT text. The architecture involves large text files representing editions and morphologically annotated texts, Python scripts to parse and yield structured data, and APIs to facilitate downstream analytic or visualization tasks. The system exhibits moderate connascence with tight coupling between raw data files (textual bases and morphological tags) and parsing routines, risking brittleness on format changes. Overall test coverage is minimal, suggesting potential risks in regression or data integrity verification. Purpose includes facilitating modern digital editions supporting textual criticism and editorial decisions linked to the SBLGNT’s eclectic text stance.",
